nt to honor my contract  the signal is i'm done in pittsburgh and  maybe done for good and they won't just  say keep the 12 and a half million  dollars and i think the best way to do  it if if that's what he wants to do  the most productive way to do it chris  is for his agent to go to the team and  say  look  he wants to retire but he doesn't want  to pay back the 12 and a half million so  we've got two ways we can do this  um he can retire and you can agree not  to take back the money or  he can force you to take a 41.25 million  dollar cap hit as of march 17. and yeah  he'll come back for one more year and  you got to pay him another 19 million  you got to deal with that cap charge all  year long what do you prefer and i think  that if they negotiate the right way  right maybe he can't walk away without  having to pay back the money if that's  what he wants i i i would agree with you  there i would think that's kind of how  that conversation goes down i i think  big ben going to another football team  is off the table uh justin and just my  assessment as the football player i  think you'd have to be  you know rivers brady  you know they were still making plays  last year  we limped into the finish line with with  with big ben  you know  it's it's like i think he has one more  year left in him definitely so that's  where i think it's a little different  you know i i don't think people are  gonna come away watching film and going  man  we need more of those four yard passes  that big ben throws you know that's  where he still can win and do that  but as big ben or you heard mike tomlin  talk about there  there's got to be a  major shift in how they approach the  game on the offensive side of the ball  they have no chance of going to a super  bowl if they're going to play the same  style they played this year next year  with big bed like a guy who can't move  and an arm is declining and we're going  to ask him to throw the ball 45 times a  game that makes no sense i